WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.340
When you head under the sea, sometimes&nbsp;
magic happens in unexpected ways. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.660
surprise cameo in The Little Mermaid has&nbsp;
fans singing with joy. Spoilers ahead!

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.560
The live-action remake of "The Little&nbsp;
Mermaid" boasts an impressive cast and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:19.140
dazzling musical numbers led by Halle Bailey's&nbsp;
acclaimed performance as Ariel. So far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.100
fans on Twitter have had positive reactions&nbsp;
that align with the early reactions from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.840
critics and moviegoers. They also praise&nbsp;
Melissa McCarthy's lively portrayal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.920
Ursula the sea witch, as well as&nbsp;
a surprising and delightful cameo.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.800
The original animated classic premiered in 1989&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.180
and introduced Ariel as a beloved icon.&nbsp;
Given the importance of the character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.460
it was only right to include a very special guest&nbsp;
during the second half of the 2023 reimagining.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.740
After Ursula's sinister spell transforms the young&nbsp;
mermaid, Ariel ascends to the surface of the ocean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.900
on her new legs. She reconnects with Prince Eric&nbsp;
and enjoys a colorful day in the royal kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.300
while sampling the many offerings on land. Among&nbsp;
the welcoming locals, one helpful vendor happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.340
to be none other than Jodi Benson, who voiced&nbsp;
Ariel in the original animated treasure.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.760
Even though Ariel is unable to&nbsp;
speak during this exciting exchange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.680
Jodi Benson's captivating presence more than&nbsp;
makes up for it. It isn't immediately clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.760
that Benson is playing the market vendor,&nbsp;
but the sound of the original Ariel's voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.480
will certainly have the audience's&nbsp;
ears perked up before her big reveal.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.600
"I get recognized a lot as the voice of her."

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.100
She holds up a fork and tells Ariel she&nbsp;
may be needing it — Ariel then misuses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.120
the renowned "dinglehopper" by running it&nbsp;
through her hair. In both versions of "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.720
Little Mermaid," the seagull Scuttle&nbsp;
mistakes the instrument for a comb.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.260
"Just a little twirl here&nbsp;
and a yank there and viola."

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:44.700
As Benson gives her the fitting gift, it&nbsp;
also feels like a passing of the torch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.660
moment between the two actresses that&nbsp;
crowns Bailey as the new Ariel. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.620
loving inclusion pays tribute to Benson's&nbsp;
heartfelt depiction while also celebrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:57.420
Bailey's groundbreaking role. In a story about&nbsp;
combining two worlds, this is a wonderful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.020
interaction that seamlessly threads the two&nbsp;
versions of "The Little Mermaid" together.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.760
The scene in which Halle Bailey's Ariel receives&nbsp;
the dinglehopper was always present in the script,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.860
but the idea of bringing Benson in manifested&nbsp;
a bit later. While discussing her cameo with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.640
Entertainment Weekly, Benson expressed just&nbsp;
how excited she was to return to the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.080
of "The Little Mermaid" and work with director&nbsp;
Rob Marshall, her friend for over four decades.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.880
"It was just a huge thrill for me when Robbie&nbsp;
reached out. I'm like, 'Of course I'm gonna come!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.720
I don't care what I'm doing. I just can't wait to&nbsp;
get around the set and watch all of you work.'"

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.380
For Marshall, it was important to fold&nbsp;
Benson into the film in a way that felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.220
organic and not "stunt-y." The director&nbsp;
also told the outlet that having the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.640
Ariels on set was a major win that&nbsp;
brought the cast and crew together.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.540
"The Little Mermaid" continues to&nbsp;
receive praise for its lead performances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.220
with Halle Bailey consistently singled out for&nbsp;
her take on Ariel. While Bailey is receiving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.600
her fair share of love from Disney fans across&nbsp;
the world, it's Jodi Benson's approval that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.220
her jumping for joy. Bailey talked about Benson&nbsp;
in a chat with the Los Angeles Times, saying:

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.220
"She told me how proud she was of&nbsp;
me and how I'm handling everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.440
and encouraged me to just go for it. I appreciate&nbsp;
her for being so warm and welcoming to me because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.920
she's the GOAT, and it was important&nbsp;
to me to get her stamp of approval."

